# Gitignored files to copy into each new worktree.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so nothing gitignored comes with it. Most of
# what this repo ignores is regenerable — node_modules/ is a 17ms `bun install`
# away, and dist/ is a build. These three are not: they hold state that exists
# only on this machine, and their absence is silent rather than loud.
#
# .gitignore syntax. Only files that match AND are gitignored are copied, so
# nothing tracked is ever duplicated.

# The never-publish list, and the reason this file exists at all.
# `publication:check` reports "no terms declared - nothing to enforce" and
# EXITS 0 when it is missing. So a worktree without it does not fail the leak
# gate — it passes it, vacuously, which is the worst way to pass a gate whose
# whole job is to stop an employer's codename reaching a public site.
content/config/corpus-guard.local.yaml

# Real Cloudflare bindings. wrangler.example.toml is committed and this is not,
# so a worktree otherwise has an example where the account expects an account.
wrangler.toml

# Per-developer Claude Code settings. Without it a worktree silently drops your
# permission and hook overrides, and behaves unlike the checkout you left.
.claude/settings.local.json
